The repository contains no Plaud code, assets or binaries. The build
downloads the official Plaud Desktop release from Plaud's servers on the
user's machine, verifies it against the checksum Plaud publishes, and
modifies a copy for local use. Applications and packages produced by the
build contain that proprietary Plaud code: they are for the use of the
person who built them and must not be redistributed. Use of Plaud is
subject to Plaud's terms of service.

Builds also bundle Electron (MIT License, https://www.electronjs.org/),
whose distribution includes Chromium and third-party components under
their own licenses (LICENSE and LICENSES.chromium.html in the application
directory). The native audio module statically links WebRTC Audio
Processing (BSD-3-Clause, https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/pulseaudio/webrtc-audio-processing)
and Abseil (Apache-2.0, https://abseil.io/).

Packages produced by the build use the system's ffmpeg at run time; no
ffmpeg binaries are distributed.
